// console.timeStamp, console.profile and console.profileEnd. No standard
// defines them: the WHATWG Console Standard's namespace (specs/idl/console.idl)
// has none of the three. All three browsers ship them, so golden rule 2 (no
// spec; the browsers agree) adds them:
//
// - Gecko, dom/webidl/Console.webidl, under its "Mozilla only or Webcompat
//   methods" comment: timeStamp(optional any data), profile(any... data),
//   profileEnd(any... data).
// - WebKit, Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/ConsoleObject.cpp: finishCreation
//   registers "timeStamp", "profile" and "profileEnd" on the console object.
// - Chrome: V8's console builtins (console.timeStamp, console.profile,
//   console.profileEnd).
//
// The signatures are Gecko's. Chrome's DevTools extensibility arguments to
// timeStamp (start, end, track, track group, color) are accepted as extra
// arguments, as every JavaScript call accepts them. Angular's DevTools
// performance integration spies on console.timeStamp (lane tpf: 10 of
// Angular's acceptance tests failed on "timeStamp() method does not exist").
partial namespace console {
  undefined timeStamp(optional any data);
  undefined profile(any... data);
  undefined profileEnd(any... data);
};
